ed dependencies, and network disabled (so any models/datasets must be assumed available locally or treated as out-of-scope for design), and (c) how the design remains valid as a design-only deliverable without executed runs (e.g., reliance on reported numbers from cited sources vs. a fully specified protocol for hypothetical execution). Keep the report focused and structured under these three headers; do not write the deliverable yet.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"For commonsense evaluations, will FuseLLM outperform Llama-2 on standard benchmarks CommenSense(CS) (zero-shot)?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"iclr2024/18013/1:setup_2\", \"iclr2024/18013/1:setup_9\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
