text\":\"Chat/instruct variants of the four constituents and Llama-2-7B-Chat are evaluated under `num_fewshot=0` in their never-prompted base mode for the chat-vs-base control, i.e., what lm-evaluation-harness reports as base-model behaviour even for a chat-tuned weight release.</item>\"},\"$text\":\"Fusion procedure in the FuseLLM paper consists of (i) continuous-weight averaging of input sub-matrices and (ii) next-token-distribution fusion via output-side weighting; for the per-source attribution the design treats these as conceptually separable so that the input-only-average can serve as a null comparator if disambiguation is required.</item>\"},\"$text\":\"OpenBookQA is treated as an 8th task for a held-out probe only and is excluded from the primary 7-task mean, per locked policy 2.</item>\"},\"$text\":\"Llama-2-7B-hf is the public checkpoint identifier used for the baseline; specific revision SHA is left to be pinned at execution time.</item>\"},\"$text\":\"lm-evaluation-harness loglikelihood-of-completion ranking is the canonical zero-shot scoring for the 7 tasks; assumed to be the protocol the FuseLLM paper used, consistent with the prompt template conventions observed in their released evaluation code.</item>\"},\"$text\":\"Numerical values in §8.1 are derived from the FuseLLM paper (Wan et al., ICLR 2024, Table 1) and are cited as approximate; exact decimals must be lifted from the paper PDF before the deliverable is published or used as evidence.</item>\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"Whether the existence of FuseLLM-13B models in the Wan et al. paper should be acknowledged in the design as an out-of-scope expansion that the study does not contradict but also does not use for the head-to-head cell.</item>\",\"$text\":\"Whether the chat-vs-base control materially changes the verdict; if Llama-2-7B-Chat substantially trails Llama-2-7B base on CS, the family alpha shifts and the head-to-head language in the delivera